Z||000057||theogre||09-15-2001||04:57 PM||||Just in case someone needs the info... I had my pedal out to replace the bushings so I measured in.... (That high pitched creaking was really annoying.... Now I just have to do the seat rails...)<P>On center measure, Pivot to MC pin, 67mm<BR>Pivot center to pedal center, 270mm. That puts you right over where the pad is welded to the arm.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">    <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><P><BR>The calculator says that's 4.02985074626865671641791044776119 to 1. My guess for the brake upgrade article was allot closer than I would have thought... The exact ratio will vary slightly depending on just how your foot rests on the pedal. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-15-2001).]||||reg||1
